{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c67f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d381-286a-7d03-bf7e-13c4c16a42b5"},"sequence":410,"recorded_at":1780531400000815,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4603a868-01f4-4025-8e84-c5ce1f2882d9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4603a868-01f4-4025-8e84-c5ce1f2882d9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4603a868-01f4-4025-8e84-c5ce1f2882d9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d382-1ce3-72d3-9f30-ccd3aad8d354"},"task_id":"01a0d382-1ce3-72d3-9f30-ccd3aad8d354","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d382-1ce3-72d3-9f30-ccd3aad8d354","chunk":"Read text file `internal/cloneplanning/text.go`.\n1|package cloneplanning\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n5|)\n6|\n7|// This file carries the single text-validity gate every exported\n8|// entry routes its consumed text through: SPEC.v0.7.0.md:256\n9|// (\"text MUST be valid UTF-8\"). encoding/json silently rewrites\n10|// invalid UTF-8 as U+FFFD and succeeds, so any entry that encodes\n11|// must refuse before the encoding step; entries that decide only\n12|// refuse with the same gate before their vocabulary gates. Text\n13|// the entry ignores (non-fact payload members in ClassifyItem)\n14|// never reaches a decision or an output, so no entry ever returns\n15|// a value whose text differs from its input.\n16|\n17|// validText reports whether the field is valid UTF-8. Every\n18|// exported entry with a text-carrying parameter applies it to the\n19|// text it consumes; the census test pins that entry set and the\n20|// refusal table pins the refusal at every entry.\n21|func validText(field string) bool {\n22|\treturn utf8.ValidString(field)\n23|}","final_result":true}}}
