{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c911","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d381-286a-7d03-bf7e-13c4c16a42b5"},"sequence":739,"recorded_at":1780531400001473,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4603a868-01f4-4025-8e84-c5ce1f2882d9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4603a868-01f4-4025-8e84-c5ce1f2882d9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4603a868-01f4-4025-8e84-c5ce1f2882d9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d387-1a50-7681-aa6d-b52117795fd4"},"task_id":"01a0d387-1a50-7681-aa6d-b52117795fd4","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d387-1a50-7681-aa6d-b52117795fd4","chunk":"Read text file `internal/cloneplanning/testdata/mutant_harness.py`.\n1|#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2|\"\"\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/cloneplanning.\n3|\n4|Every gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present and is\n5|weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject,\n6|and the named killer test must fail when run alone. A delete-only\n7|mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as\n8|evidence.\n9|\n10|Each row runs M (mutate one production file in place), R (run the\n11|scoped Go killer through a production entry), V (verdict from the Go\n12|exit code plus a FAIL kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test\n13|failure line, SURVIVED iff R passes, ERROR for anything else --\n14|unapplied patches, build breaks, timeouts). M failures and R\n15|infrastructure errors are ERROR, never kills or survivals. The file\n16|is restored from its backup after every row, pass or fail.\n17|\n18|Shared gates (the checkItem vocabulary and fact gates with two call\n19|sites: PlanItem and ClassifyItem) carry one plant each with the\n20|both-entries killer TestSharedItemVocabBothEntries.\n21|\n22|Row N-visible-escape-suffix is the token-preserving attack: the\n23|JSON token still leads the output but the behavior changes, and the\n24|killer executes the behavioral escaping suite.\n25|\n26|Single-member-class rows narrow a gate whose reject class holds\n27|exactly one member, so the plant admits the whole class, which is\n28|one member.\n29|\n30|Row C-doc-comment is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that\n31|must SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\n32|hard-coding kills.\n33|\n34|Usage:\n35|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/cloneplanning/testdata/mutant_harness.py [--log-dir DIR] [MUTANT ...]\n36|\"\"\"\n37|\n38|import shutil\n39|import subprocess\n40|import sys\n41|import tempfile\n42|import time\n43|from dataclasses import dataclass\n44|from pathlib import Path\n45|\n46|REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\n47|PACKAGE = \"internal/cloneplanning\"\n48|\n49|\n50|@dataclass(frozen=True)\n51|class Mutant:\n52|    name: str\n53|    path: str\n54|    find: str\n55|    replace: str\n56|    count: int\n57|    run: str\n58|    expect: str\n59|    note: str\n60|\n61|\n62|MUTANTS = [\n63|    Mutant(\n64|        name=\"N-select-archive-priority\",\n65|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/strategy.go\",\n66|        find='''\\tif archive {\\n\\t\\treturn strategyArchive, nil\\n\\t}\\n\\tif continuation {\\n\\t\\treturn strategyContinuation, nil\\n\\t}''',\n67|        replace='''\\tif continuation {\\n\\t\\treturn strategyContinuation, nil\\n\\t}\\n\\tif archive {\\n\\t\\treturn strategyArchive, nil\\n\\t}''',\n68|        count=1,\n69|        run=\"TestSelectStrategyOracle\",\n70|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n71|        note=\"Narrows the priority gate: archive+continuation selects continuation instead of archive.\",\n72|    ),\n73|    Mutant(\n74|        name=\"N-select-official\",\n75|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/strategy.go\",\n76|        find='''\\tif !sameEnvironment {\\n\\t\\tif officialImport {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn strategyOfficial, nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn strategyNativeWriter, nil\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn strategyNativeRewrite, nil''',\n77|        replace='''\\tif officialImpor