alid bytes cannot change the item | CI, PI, TE, PV | TestClassifyItemIgnoresPayloadTextAllKinds (8432 sealed + 1054 hand-built + 1581 generated/long, downstream chain to zero, reviewer probes through PV); TestClassifyItemIgnoresInvalidPayloadBytes (620 cells); TestClassifyItemReadsClosedFactsOnly (AST); TestClassifyItemVocabMatchesSpec (spec pin); TestProjectVisibleWholeDomain, TestProjectVisiblePositionIndependence; SS/SP/PI/PS/TE take no text by type |\n48|| 13 | Tools inert; pending blocked | TE, PI | TestPlanTargetEffectsZeroSweep, TestPlanTargetEffectsChained |\n49|| 14 | Source usage never target accounting | TE | TestPlanTargetEffectsZeroSweep (556 mappings + per-disposition) |\n50|| 15 | Token classes (control-token text + usage counts) | PV, TE | rows 11 + 14 probes |\n51|| 16 | Vendor importer strategy arm | PI | TestPlanItemImporterRule |\n52|| 17 | Session counts + empty/1M/1M+1 edges | PS | TestPlanSessionCounts, TestPlanSessionRefusals, TestPlanSessionMillionEdge |\n53|| 18 | Importer grid base vs candidate, moved classes named | — | importer-grid.log, byte-identity (232 files, 0 differ, moved none) |\n54|\n55|Stated bounds (not waived): operation synthesis; source/target\n56|condition reasons outside the item axis; capability-gated\n57|degradation past tool/subagent importer classes; per-kind\n58|text-field extraction (visible entry takes extracted typed texts);\n59|full Migration Checkpoint sealing; fact-name renames past the\n60|grep pin; invalid UTF-8 in ignored payload members (accepted and\n61|ignored, never decided or emitted); delegating outer UTF-8 checks\n62|as defense in depth (inner gate measured). See TRACEABILITY.md.\n63|\n64|## Mutant evidence (UTF-8 rows; full battery below)\n65|\n66|| Mutant | What it narrows the gate to | Named test that fails (run alone) |\n67||---|---|---|\n68|| N-escape-utf8-fffe | Direct escaping entry admits exactly the ff-fe member; encoding/json then succeeds with a U+FFFD value | TestEscapeVisibleTextRefusesInvalidUTF8 |\n69|| N-select-profile-utf8 | Profile selection admits exactly the ff-fe member; the vocabulary fallback refuses with another message | TestSelectProfileRefusesInvalidUTF8 |\n70|| N-visible-utf8 (anchor moved to shared gate) | ProjectVisibleText loop skips exactly field[1]; the direct entry refuses with the unindexed message | TestProjectVisibleTextRefusals |\n71|\n72|No survivors among narrowings. The neutral control\n73|`C-doc-comment` (comment-only edit) SURVIVED as designed in all\n74|three battery runs, proving the harness observes outcomes. Full\n75|battery: 52 KILLED + 1 SURVIVED, 0 mismatches, 0 errors, three\n76|runs (`harness1/`, `harness2/` on the pre-probe tree,\n77|`harness3/` on the final tree; the delta between them is one\n78|added assertion cell in the escape killer, re-verified alone).\n79|\n80|## Validation (real exit codes)\n81|\n82|| Command | Exit | Evidence |\n83||---|---|---|\n84|| `go test -count=1 -v ./internal/cloneplanning/` | 0 | `package.log` |\n85|| `go test -count=1 -cover ./internal/cloneplanning/` | 0, 98.1% statements | `cover.log` |\n86|| `go test -count=3` on the 11 new tests | 0 | `determinism.log` |\n87|| `go test -race -count=1 ./internal/cloneplanning/` | 0 | `race-package.log` |\n88|| `go test -p 4 -count=1` on the 9 owner packages | 0, 9 ok | `owners.log` |\n89|| `go test -p 2 -count=1` full suite, 4 shards | 0, 48 ok, 0 FAIL | `full-shard1.log` .. `full-shard4.log` |\n90|| 17 configured `go test -fuzz ... -fuzztime=100x` commands | 0 all | `fuzz.log` |\n91|| `go vet ./...` | 0 | `vet.log` |\n92|| `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` | 0 | `winvet.log` |\n93|| configured `test -z \"$(gofmt -l ...)\"` | 0, no files | `gofmt.log` |\n94|| `go build ./...` | 0 | `build.log` |\n95|| `GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 | `build-linux.log` |\n96|| `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 | `build-windows.log` |\n97|| `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 | `tracecheck.log` |\n98|| `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted ... -check` | 0 | `cataloggen.log` |\n99|| configured JSON validity sweep | 0 | `jsoncheck.log` |\n100|| `task-board validate` | 0 (254 pre-existing board warnings, none on this task) | `board-validate.log` |\n101|| `git diff --check` | 0 | `diffcheck.log` |\n102|| Scratch-index `git diff --cached --check` (20 new paths) | 0 | `hygiene.log`, `scope.log` |\n103|| Mutant battery, 53 rows, run 1 | 52 KILLED + control SURVIVED, 0 mismatches | `harness1-summary.log`, `harness1/` |\n104|| Mutant battery, 53 rows, run 2 | 52 KILLED + control SURVIVED, 0 mismatches | `harness2-summary.log`, `harness2/` |\n105|| Mutant battery, 53 rows, run 3 (final tree) | 52 KILLED + control SURVIVED, 0 mismatches | `harness3-summary.log`, `harness3/` |\n106|| Census plant: new entry, no row (must redden) | 1, reflection linkage named | `census-control-plant.log` |\n107|| Census plant + reflection row (must redden at table) | 1, refusal-table linkage named | `census-control-table.log` |\n108|| Census revert (must pass, byte-identical) | 0 | `census-control-revert.log` |\n109|| Marshal guard: second call site (must redden) | 1, sites named | `guard-control-site.log` |\n110|| Marshal guard: gate removed (must redden) | 1, gate named | `guard-control-gate.log` |\n111|| Escape killer on pre-fix shape (authentic failure) | 1, admission named | `prefix-demo-killer.log` |\n112|| Owner byte-identity base vs candidate | identical, 232 files, 0 differ | `importer-grid.log` |\n113|| `git status` candidate scope | only `?? internal/cloneplanning/` | (worktree state) |\n114|| `go test ./... -cover -count=1` (full-cover) | NOT RUN | unchanged identity for 47/48 packages; changed package measured at 98.1%; rerun by CR validation |\n115|| `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` (full-race) | NOT RUN | exceeds the bounded-call budget; changed package race-green; rerun by CR validation |\n116|\n117|Shard note: `full-shard1.log` ran before the final one-cell\n118|addition to the escape killer; the rerun `package.log` covers\n119|that delta on the final tree, and the other 47 packages are\n120|byte-unchanged since their shard runs.\n121|\n122|## Out-of-contract rows (declared, not silent)\n123|\n124|- Closed shapes (plan, manifest, fidelity report, capture,\n125|  canonical): sibling leaves cloneplan/clonefidelity/clonebundle;\n126|  this leaf decides populating values, never validates shapes.\n127|- G1 normalization and folds: clonesnap/cloneproject; consumed\n128|  here by reference and source pin.\n129|- Target-branch admission: clonesnap.AdmitForTarget (caller\n130|  scope); this leaf routes the branch only.\n131|- Transaction, lineage, read-back, validation (13.14.3-13.14.5):\n132|  sibling/future scope.\n133|\n134|## Brief gap (handoff precondition 1)\n135|\n136|The brief carries no surface table, so there is no surface row to\n137|map. Coverage map substitute: the clause map in\n138|`internal/cloneplanning/TRACEABILITY.md` maps every derivation\n139|rule to its production entries and named tests, and the\n140|conformance matrix maps every gate to its entries, killer tests,\n141|and killed narrowings (52 narrowings + 1 control).\n142|\n143|## Reviewer tests kept\n144|\n145|No previously committed reviewer test exists on the board (rev1\n146|and rev3 verdicts carried probe files inside their evidence tars,\n147|not committed tests). The rev1 reviewer's exact\n148|`subagent_started` plant and all six probe texts remain embedded\n149|in the committed sweep and `N-classify-text-subagent`; the rev3\n150|reviewer's exact FF probe is now embedded in\n151|`TestEscapeVisibleTextRefusesInvalidUTF8`, so the next cycle\n152|inherits both.\n153|\n154|## Rework diff bound\n155|\n156|The rev3 -> rev4 diff touches `internal/cloneplanning/` only: 3\n157|new files (`text.go`, `utf8_test.go`, `census_test.go`), 6 edited\n158|production files (UTF-8 routing only), 1 edited harness (+2 rows,\n159|1 anchor moved to the shared gate), 1 edited TRACEABILITY rule.\n160|No file outside it is listed: no landed-file edit, no registry\n161|edit, no production-code change outside the named module.\n162|\n163|## Logbook-relevant decisions\n164|\n165|- `encoding/json.Marshal` on a Go string with invalid UTF-8\n166|  succeeds and emits U+FFFD (verified by the prefix-demo run);\n167|  every entry that encodes must therefore refuse before the\n168|  encoding step, which is what `R-UTF8` states.\n169|- `ProjectVisibleText` keeps its indexed field message distinct\n170|  from the direct entry's unindexed message; that distinction is\n171|  what keeps the field[1] narrowing observable now that both\n172|  entries gate.\n173|- Ignored payload bytes stay ignored (accepted, never decided\n174|  or emitted) rather than refused: refusal there would fork the\n175|  landed decoder's closed-shape validation into the planning\n176|  leaf.","final_result":true}}}
